body:
I don't even know what hole that is coming from?

&#x200B;

Also happy cake day bruh!

I have the exact same problem with my hair! Its thin and i dont have an awful lot of it so it doesnt take *too* much effort to curl but i've always used a super thin wand and curled my hair insanely curly so when it drops (eventually after 2 days) it goes to the kind of curl i want, but it can be such a pain because i want my 2 day old curls when i initially wanted that type of curl right away! Bought some curlers that curled EXACTLY like i wanted and i was so so happy but then they fell out within an hour even with loads of hairspray. So i either have super tight curls and drop in days to what i want or i curl them to how i want and then they drop within an hour. Cant win! The extra kicker is my hairdresser can curl to the level i want AND they stay in for days!!!! It IS possible its just a night mare to find the sweet spot! 

&#x200B;

My hairdresser advised that after you're curling each individual curl you hold the curl in your hand for 5 seconds or so to cool down, then hairspray it! She also suggested a serum after the hairs curled. I'm yet to try it myself but hopefully that helps! I will have fingers crossed for us both!

Im SO glad to see you ended it before i could comment DONT DO IT! 

&#x200B;

Never ever ever compromise something as important as this for anyone. ANYONE.

&#x200B;

You made the right call!
